# How to use the plugin and commands

## How to use /fire
How /fire works.
/fire (x) (y) (z)
You can use ~ ~ ~ for your current location
/fire (x) (y) (z) (payload)

Payload is either Nuke, Stab, and mushroom.


/fire (x) (y) (z) (payload) (fuse)

Fuse is how long the tnt will take in order to explode. 80 ticks for default fuse time

/fire (x) (y) (z) (payload) (fuse) (spacing)

Spacing is how much blocks will be apart from each ring

/fire (x) (y) (z) (payload) (fuse) (spacing) (use_motion)

Use motion is dictate if the nuke will be created using motion.

/fire (x) (y) (z) (payload) (fuse) (spacing) (motion_y)

Motion y will dictate how fast it will go down

/fire (x) (y) (z) (payload) (fuse) (spacing) (motion_y) (rings)
Rings are how many circles of tnt will be in the nuke. not neded for mushroom or stab

/fire (x) (y) (z) (payload) (fuse) (spacing) (motion_y) (rings) (tnt_per_ring)
Tnt per ring is how much tnt will be in each ring. not needed for mushroom or stab

